spans.s:
चिल् चिल्, cl. 6. P. चिलति, &c., to put on
clothes; [cf. Hib. ceilim, ‘I conceal,
hide, cover;’ caille, ‘a veil, a cowl;’ Lat. celare;
Old Germ. hilu, helm, heliu, heli; Goth. hulja;
Lat. oc-culo.]

चिल्लि, इस्, m. a species of bird of prey [cf. चिल्ल];
(इस्), f. a kind of plant [cf. चिल्ली]; (ई), f. a cricket
[cf. चिल्लका]; a kind of pot-herb.
